          <h2 class="mt-14 text-3xl font-extrabold tracking-tight text-slate-900">
            What the pre-charge is worth
          </h2>
          <p class="mt-4 text-slate-600 leading-relaxed">
            A {SHELL}-gallon tank on a 30/50 switch, with only the Schrader valve changing. The peak is at
            cut-in; the {PRECHARGE_BELOW_CUTIN_PSI} psi margin below it costs about{" "}
            {fmt((atCutIn - defaults.fraction) * 100, 1)} of a percentage point and saves the diaphragm from
            bottoming out on every cycle.
          </p>

          <div class="mt-8 overflow-x-auto rounded-2xl border border-slate-200 bg-white shadow-sm">
            <table class="w-full text-left text-sm">
              <thead>
                <tr class="border-b border-slate-200 text-slate-500 bg-slate-50">
                  <th class="py-3 px-5 font-semibold">Pre-charge</th>
                  <th class="py-3 px-5 font-semibold">Drawdown fraction</th>
                  <th class="py-3 px-5 font-semibold">{SHELL} gal tank gives</th>
                  <th class="py-3 px-5 font-semibold">Verdict</th>
                </tr>
              </thead>
              <tbody class="text-slate-700">
                {
                  prechargeTable.map((row, index) => (
                    <tr class={index === prechargeTable.length - 1 ? "" : "border-b border-slate-100"}>
                      <td class="py-3 px-5 font-semibold text-slate-900">{row.pre} psi</td>
                      <td class="py-3 px-5">{fmt(row.fraction * 100, 2)}%</td>
                      <td class="py-3 px-5">{fmt(row.delivered, 2)} gal</td>
                      <td class="py-3 px-5">
                        {row.pre === 28
                          ? "Correct"
                          : row.pre < 28
                            ? "Low — diaphragm sits compressed"
                            : row.pre === 30
                              ? "At cut-in — best on paper, hard on the bag"
                              : "Over-charged — short-cycles"}
                      </td>
                    </tr>
                  ))
                }
              </tbody>
            </table>
          </div>

          <h2 class="mt-14 text-3xl font-extrabold tracking-tight text-slate-900">Tank by pump size</h2>
          <p class="mt-4 text-slate-600 leading-relaxed">
            On a 30/50 switch, with the conventional minimum run time for each pump. The jump at 12 gpm is the
            run-time rule stepping up, not the pump.
          </p>

          <div class="mt-8 overflow-x-auto rounded-2xl border border-slate-200 bg-white shadow-sm">
            <table class="w-full text-left text-sm">
              <thead>
                <tr class="border-b border-slate-200 text-slate-500 bg-slate-50">
                  <th class="py-3 px-5 font-semibold">Pump</th>
                  <th class="py-3 px-5 font-semibold">Min run</th>
                  <th class="py-3 px-5 font-semibold">Drawdown needed</th>
